meta {
  name: Undo Approval
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{apiUrl}}/sessions/{{sessionId}}/requests/{{playerId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "PENDING"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.success: eq true
  res.body.data.status: eq PENDING
}

docs {
  Depends on **Approve Request** having run (the request must be `APPROVED` for there to
  be anything to undo). Runs as the **host**, same route/DTO as **Approve Request** --
  `PATCH /sessions/:id/requests/:userId` -- just with `"status": "PENDING"` instead of
  `"APPROVED"`/`"REJECTED"`. `SessionController.decideRequest` special-cases that value and
  routes to `UndoDecisionUseCase` instead of `DecideRequestUseCase`.

  `UndoDecisionUseCase`, approved path:
  1. Load session -> 404 if missing; caller must be `session.host.id` -> else 403 (same
     authorization as deciding in the first place).
  2. Load the request -> 404 if missing; status must be `APPROVED` or `REJECTED` -> else
     `RequestNotDecidedError` (409) -- see **Undo Decision - still pending**.
  3. `revertApproval`'s `TransactWriteItems` (the mirror image of `approveRequest`'s):
     ```
     request item:  SET #s = :pending                      IF #s = :approved
     session META:  SET slots_remaining = :n + 1, #s = OPEN IF slots_remaining = :n
                                                             AND (#s = OPEN OR #s = FULL)
     ```
     Always lands on `OPEN`, never back on `FULL` -- freeing a slot can only ever make a
     session less full. See **Get Session After Undo Approval** for the slot-count check.
}
